    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made it a returned field.\n\n**The key** (`Owner.identityKey`): `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. A new owner is rejected with **409** only when its *whole* key equals an existing owner's \u2014 so two members of the same household with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` string to the `Owner` schema, so it appears in `OwnerDto`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `static String identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)` (the single formula) and a `@Transient getIdentityKey()`. MapStruct auto-maps `getIdentityKey()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.setIdentityKey`, satisfying \"Return 'identityKey'\".\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced the three separate checks (`rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, `rejectDuplicateHousehold`) with one `rejectDuplicateIdentity(...)` that compares the new owner's key (using normalized telephone, canonical email, and the *prospective* householdId) against every existing owner's key. Removed the now-unused `findHouseholdMate` helper and `Optional` import; updated the imports and `prepareNewOwner` docs.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException.java`** \u2014 new 409-signalling exception replacing the three old ones.\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 replaced the three old handlers/constants with a single `DuplicateIdentity` \u2192 409 handler.\n- Deleted the three obsolete exception classes (`DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`); no references remain.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (same telephone \u2192 409) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is green.\n\nNote the intended behaviour change this introduces: previously, a second owner sharing another's email, or a household duplicate (same lastName+address without `sharesHousehold`), was rejected on its own. Now a collision requires the *entire* key to match \u2014 e.g. two owners with the same email but different telephones are both accepted. This is exactly what the specification asks for.",
